{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The exchange rate is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> US Dollar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b5c6469b89a9938ac7b0293dba1816afb96d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=0.94$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> euros. What is the value in dollars of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aaff8bc92f20b4eba4e69d07c4fcc53f6f99e64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$750$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> euros?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b04ca4d1d4d02a67ad251d581393934ef4a426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\  \\$705.00 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\  \\$798.00 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\  \\$795.00 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\  \\$797.87 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\  \\$750.94 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"637\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> USD is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d2758d22fa40544a82f0f42458e1d6d787a3ee2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.94$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> euros, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/3/ab35edbf9d3d91a6b4b044c294d4254bd1222e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{0.94}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" /> USD must be equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> euro. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aaff8bc92f20b4eba4e69d07c4fcc53f6f99e64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$750$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> euros is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6eff5a7c729dbf67b46ddfbc4cc505cf5a7857c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{750}{0.94}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" /> USD, which is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db989111ab55dde7e3afe5a8103b9112efd0947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } \\$797.87}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"109\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_I_Contest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra I Contest Answer